WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.480
<v Dana>Thanks for joining the Riverside Library steering meeting.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.460
<v Dana>First item is the renovation schedule.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.600
<v Mats>The contractor confirmed the scaffolding comes down on the ninth of March.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.500
<v Mats>After that the electricians need about three weeks on the upper floor.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.320
<v Priya>Does that move the reopening of the children's wing?

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:29.920
<v Mats>Not yet. The children's wing still reopens on the twelfth of May.

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:34.160
<v Dana>Good. What about the budget for the reading room furniture?

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.640
<v Priya>We approved forty-two thousand pounds for furniture in January.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:43.180
<v Priya>The supplier quote came in at thirty-nine thousand five hundred,

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:47.240
<v Priya>so we have about two and a half thousand left for lamps.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.000
<v Dana>Let's keep that margin until the lamps are ordered.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:55.120
<v Mats>One risk: the lift parts are delayed by the manufacturer.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:00.200
<v Mats>If they arrive after April, the second floor stays closed to wheelchairs.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:04.140
<v Dana>Can we hire a temporary stair climber in the meantime?

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:08.500
<v Priya>The council lends one for free if we book it two weeks ahead.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.540
<v Dana>Please book it from the first of April.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.740
<v Priya>Will do.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.080
<v Dana>Next item is the opening hours consultation.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.140
<v Mats>We had three hundred and eighty responses to the survey.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:26.340
<v Mats>Most people asked for late opening on Thursdays until eight in the evening.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.240
<v Priya>Weekend mornings came second, mostly from parents with young children.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:36.200
<v Dana>So the proposal is Thursday evenings and an earlier start on Saturdays.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:41.280
<v Mats>Staffing for Thursdays needs one extra librarian on a part-time contract.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:45.220
<v Dana>I'll take that to the staffing panel on the twentieth.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.160
<v Priya>Before we move on, the café tender closed last Friday.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.880
<v Priya>Two bids came in, and the lower one is from Harbour Street Kitchen.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:58.240
<v Mats>Their bid includes running the café on Thursday evenings too.

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:00.800
<v Dana>That fits the new hours nicely.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:05.280
<v Dana>Let's ask procurement to check their food hygiene rating first.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.660
<v Mats>Last item: the archive move.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:12.020
<v Mats>The local history archive goes to the basement store in June,

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.660
<v Mats>once the dehumidifiers have run for a full month.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:20.260
<v Priya>The volunteers want a list of boxes that need conservation first.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.900
<v Mats>I can share the box list by the end of next week.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.400
<v Dana>Thank you. Any other business?

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:31.240
<v Priya>Only that the opening event is pencilled in for the sixteenth of May,

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.580
<v Priya>four days after the children's wing reopens.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.280
<v Dana>Let's confirm the date once the lift parts arrive.

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:41.440
<v Mats>Agreed. I'll update the risk log tonight.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.320
<v Dana>Then we'll meet again in two weeks. Thanks, everyone.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.640
<v Mats>One more thing on the lift.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:53.140
<v Mats>The manufacturer now promises delivery in the week of the twenty-third of March.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.380
<v Priya>That would leave enough time for the inspection before May.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.960
<v Dana>Good, then the stair climber is only a fallback.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.600
<v Priya>I'll keep the booking but mark it as provisional.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.520
<v Dana>Perfect. That's everything for today.
